# decision_rule (verbatim PLAN-X01-v5.1 line 65): 1. **Freeze.** Script SHA256 into `<name>.prereg.sha256` (project convention, root; `#` header lines + hash lines incl. imports and data) BEFORE the run. A frozen script is never edited; a change = new versioned file. No result overwrite; new run ids only.
# decision_rule (verbatim PLAN-X01-v5.1 line 66): 2. **Gate math, 9 cells (checked by IV).** A gate needs >=10/15 folds (or books) in each of 9 cells (3 transliterations x 3 gate seeds). One cell: p=0.733 per fold clears 81.2%, p=0.8 clears 93.9%. Nine cells if independent: p=0.733 -> 15%; p=0.8 -> 57%; p=0.84 -> 81%; 80% needs p ~0.837. Folds, seeds and transliterations share data, so real odds are lower. **Strictness is intended:** a failed gate costs coverage (UNINFORMATIVE), never a false call. An "at most 4/15 in all 9 cells" control: per-fold match 0.1 -> passes 89.1%; 0.2 -> 19.9% (both recomputed).
# decision_rule (verbatim PLAN-X01-v5.1 line 67): 3. **Dev vs gate seeds + guard.** Everything is tuned only on dev seeds. Gate seeds are different (3a). Enforcement, exact check: the shared module `vx01_common.py` (frozen first, script 0) embeds `GATE_SEED_SHA256`, the SHA256 of EACH gate seed written as decimal text (all 156 gate seeds of 3a: 3 B0, 75 A1, 60 A2, 15 A4, 3 B2; the seeds are public in 3a anyway, the hashes make the check explicit). (a) In dev mode every seed given to a vx01 script is hashed; if SHA256(str(seed)) is in `GATE_SEED_SHA256` the script exits 3 before doing anything. (b) Gate mode needs `--gate`. It then (i) recomputes SHA256 of its own source, of `vx01_common.py`, of `vx01_gate_seeds.json` and of its own dev log (rule 4) and compares each with the stub lines `script_sha256=`, `common_sha256=`, `gate_seeds_sha256=`, `dev_log_sha256=`; (ii) checks every seed in `vx01_gate_seeds.json` hashes into `GATE_SEED_SHA256` (no other seed can be a gate seed); any mismatch or missing stub exits 3 before any gate seed is used. (c) It prints all hashes and `stub_match` in the result header. This is code discipline, not cryptographic; IV recomputes the hashes independently.
# decision_rule (verbatim PLAN-X01-v5.1 line 68): 4. **Dev-run log, one per script.** Each script appends only to its OWN log `vx01_<name>_dev_runs.log` (name = the top-level script that was started; a script that imports another frozen script never writes to that script's log). Each line: UTC time, script SHA256, arguments, seeds, SHA256 of each output file, SHA256 of the previous line (hash chain). The stub of script X fixes `dev_log_sha256=` = SHA256 of X's whole log file at freeze time. A later dev run of any OTHER script appends to a different file, so it cannot change X's log or break X's stub; a dev run of X after its stub is forbidden (it would change X's log hash and `--gate` would refuse). `vx01_common.py` is frozen before every other script and its hash is in every stub, so it never changes afterwards. **"Max 2 revisions"** covers code bugs and the fitter procedure only, each a new versioned file, all attempts kept; it NEVER covers thresholds, MEI, bands, decision rules, seeds, spread tables or family pairings. A change there = new plan id; the failure stays on record. **Gate runs (IV v3 item 4).** A `--gate` run appends to a SEPARATE file `vx01_<name>_gate_runs.log`, which is NOT hashed in the stub. So the dev log stays hash-checkable (its final hash is in the stub and no gate run touches it) and `--gate` checks still work (they read only the dev log, the script, `vx01_common.py` and the gate-seed file). The gate log has the same line format, hash-chained, with a start line (`GATE-START`) and an end line (`GATE-COMPLETE`) that carries the SHA256 of each result file. A gate run is single-shot per frozen script: `--gate` refuses (exit 3) if the gate log already holds a `GATE-COMPLETE` for this `script_sha256`. A crash (start without complete) may be rerun with identical code; every earlier `GATE-START` is counted and printed in the result header. The final gate-log hash is printed in the result file and filed with the result (not in the stub).
# decision_rule (verbatim PLAN-X01-v5.1 line 69): 5. **Target power 0.8 and MEI** stated per test before running; planted effect = MEI. Fixture miss => UNINFORMATIVE.
# decision_rule (verbatim PLAN-X01-v5.1 line 70): 6. **Thresholds.** F1 >=0.85, exact triple >=0.70, null false-structure <=5%, >=10/15 are ARBITRARY BUT FIXED before any run, confirmed by Eve 2026-10-18 22:17 PDT, not tuned on data. Link to A2: F1 0.85 allows about 15% boundary error, so A2 injects error at the measured e and at 1.5 x e. The 10/15 gate is the project's D-068 rule.
# decision_rule (verbatim PLAN-X01-v5.1 line 71): 7. A flip under a segmenter counts as evidence only if that segmenter is ADEQUATE ON PLANTED BOOKS (A1).
# decision_rule (verbatim PLAN-X01-v5.1 line 72): 8. ZL3b primary, RF1b and IT2a replication. Part A re-runs on real findings (A3) copy each finding's frozen call and thresholds verbatim from its original stub. Part B does NOT carry over old thresholds: only the project's 10/15 and 4/15 counts (rule 2); see section 5. Compute: <=2 BelowNormal workers, only after current jobs finish; I do not touch the ~17 running jobs.
