# decision_rule (verbatim PLAN-X01-v5.1 line 95): **Recount.** Total 192 seeds, all distinct (checked: no overlap between any two lists, none shared between dev and gate). Gate seeds 156 (B0 3, A1 75 = 5 lists x 15, A2 60 = 4 x 15, A4 15, B2 3); their 156 SHA256 values are embedded in `vx01_common.py`. Dev seeds 36 (B0 3, A1 5, A2 20, A4 5, B2 3). Per script: `vx01_a1_*` dev 5 / gate 75; `vx01_a2_*` dev 20 / gate 60; `vx01_a3_*` none (re-runs of real findings use each original frozen call's own seeds, verbatim; no new random seed); `vx01_a4_*` dev 5 / gate 15; `vx01_b0_*` and `vx01_b1_*` dev 3 / gate 3 (B1 uses the B0 gate seeds, real data adds none); `vx01_b2_*` dev 3 / gate 3; `vx01_seg_mdl.py` deterministic, no seed. A2 corruption randomness derives from the book seed by the fixed rule above (text includes the corruption level), so it adds no seeds.
